3way-mpi - MPI Implementation
==============================
------------------------------
Running Manually (for testing)
------------------------------
    mpirun -np <num_processes> ./3way-mpi <input_file> [batch_size]

Example:
    mpirun -np 4 ./3way-mpi /homes/eyv/cis520/wiki_dump.txt

Optional batch_size argument controls how many lines are read at once
(default: 50000).

------------------------------
Scheduling on Beocat via Slurm
------------------------------
Edit run.sh to set your desired configuration:

    #SBATCH --nodes=<num_nodes>
    #SBATCH --ntasks-per-node=<cores_per_node>
    #SBATCH --mem-per-cpu=<memory>    (e.g. 1G, 512M, 64M)
    #SBATCH --time=<hh:mm:ss>

Submit a single job:

    sbatch run.sh

Submit multiple runs for statistical analysis:

    for i in $(seq 1 10); do sbatch run.sh; done

------------------------------
Output
------------------------------
- logs/mpi-%j.out        stdout log for each job
- logs/mpi-n*-c*-m*-*.err   real/user/sys timing for each job
- logs/output_<job_id>.txt   full program output for each job

To view timing results across all runs:

    grep -H "real\|user\|sys" logs/*.err
